# AA-993 V2 (ADR 0016 D3) — HTTP rows of the CRM api post-deploy verify (service aa-crm-dev-api), read by
# .github/scripts/post_deploy_verify.sh.
#
# One row per line: name|auth|METHOD path|expected HTTP|jq assertion
#   auth       public only (the one machine route, /crm/ci/deploy-gate, takes a GitHub OIDC token minted for
#              deploy-dev.yml alone, so the verify cannot call it)
#   METHOD     GET only (the verify never writes)
#   assertion  a jq expression on the response body that must be true; empty = only the HTTP code is checked.
#              Variables: $sha (deployed commit), $version (.release-please-manifest.json of that commit),
#              $required (the newest crm-NNN in REQUIRED_SCHEMA_VERSIONS of api/app/db.py of that commit).
# A row fails after 3 tries. A PR that adds or changes an endpoint worth guarding adds a row here.
#
# The ECS rows (rollout COMPLETED, desired >= 1, image = <registry>/<repo>:<sha>) are fixed in the script.
# /crm/health/ready answers 200 only when every crm-NNN the running code needs is registered; the assertion also
# pins the prefix and checks that the newest registered key is at least the newest one of the deployed commit.

health|public|GET /crm/health|200|.status == "ok" and .service == "aa-crm-api" and .git_sha == $sha and .version == $version
health-ready|public|GET /crm/health/ready|200|.status == "ok" and .db == "ok" and ((.schema_version // "") | test("^crm-[0-9]+$")) and ((.schema_version | ltrimstr("crm-") | tonumber) >= ($required | ltrimstr("crm-") | tonumber))
